  "note": "The core is the Cadmium emulator's machines (MIT) built with this repository's patches (MIT) and integration (MIT). Compiled in with it: Chiplet, {fmt}, the ghc filesystem and utility headers, nlohmann/json and magic_enum (all MIT); fast_float (MIT, Apache-2.0 or BSL-1.0, at the user's choice); bit-lite (BSL-1.0); a SHA-1 implementation, stdendian and stb_image (public domain). Chiplet's Octo compiler is a C++ version of the one in John Earnest's C-Octo (MIT). Cadmium's source contains, as data, the small programs the emulated computers were sold or published with: the COSMAC VIP's monitor and RCA's CHIP-8 interpreters (1977-78), and CHIPOS for the DREAM 6800 (Michael J. Bauer, 1978, used by Cadmium with his permission) with Tobias V. Langhoff's CHIPOSLO. The package contains no CHIP-8 program.",
